# ai-copilots (library operator harness)

When creating or migrating a library's agent harness, editing `AGENTS.md` /
`ai-copilots/**`, or wiring a Go dependency's skills into a host IDE:

- If `AGENTS.md` or `ai-copilots/` is missing, load skill `ai-readiness`
  first (and load skill `ai-readiness-persona` when a setup fork exists).
- Load skill `author-ai-copilots` (templates in `reference.md`).
- Load skill `agent-smith` when authoring or reviewing skill bodies.
- If editing pack-owned files under `.cursor/packs/shared/`, follow skill `edit-cursor-packs`.

Resolve module Dir with `go list -m -f '{{.Dir}}' <module-path>` before host symlinks.
Prefer symlink/junction to in-module `ai-copilots/`; do not copy skill bodies without approval.
When adding fire-and-forget wires under `.cursor/skills/` or `.cursor/rules/`, load `cursor-wired-discovery.mdc` and run `sync-wired-cursor-gitignore.sh`.
